[Music]  hotline Miami - wrong numbers action is  so loud and so intense that upon hitting  the pause button reality feels like it's  playing at half speed this is the type  of experience that invites you in to sit  closer to the screen and crank up the  volume higher than usual one of the  lingering memories of the first game was  its heart pounding techno soundtrack so  yeah allow me to get this edit away  early the music and hotline Miami -  wrong number is absolutely outstanding  but to revel in this game slick style  too much would be a disservice to its  ferociously entertaining and challenging  top-down action this is a confident  follow-up which approves upon the  original in almost every conceivable way  hotline Miami - is more varied better  paced and more challenging this is a  tremendously stylish game which  entertains throughout and delights in  forcing you out of your comfort zone  [Music]  [Music]  hotline Miami - wrong number is a  top-down twitch shooter in which you  play a host of psychopaths for an  assortment of reasons are required to  enter various buildings and kill  everyone therein they achieve this using  a variety of weapons shotguns automatic  rifles silenced pistols and even their  fists but regardless of the delivery  methods death comes quickly don't expect  to soak up damage or pick up health  packs here this is a game where a single  bullets can kill you and your foes we're  on the toes tactics and a quick trigger  finger can be the difference between you  completing a level and topping order to  respawn over and over and over how you  choose to clear each area in the game's  30 or so levels is largely up to you you  can run and gun with reckless abandon or  say use a loud shotgun burst to learn  nearby enemies into your path whatever  you choose the engagements are  exhilarating though planning your attack  will net the best results the intense  visuals thumping soundtrack and score  multiplier will seduce you into risking  it all for one glorious foolhardy charge  clever level design and increased enemy  variety make these engagements more  interesting than before halls and rooms  have more interesting angles extra  windows more open areas and multiple  lanes for enemies to approach from what  better enemy placement creates increased  diversity in the types of engagements  you'll encounter the melee resistant  dogs return as did the fad enemies which  are impervious to anything other than  bullets but they're joined by a bullet  docking Samurai running enemies who leap  to close the distance and a selection of  level specific mini bosses in fact  variety is what hotline Miami 2 is all  about while the first game was largely  centered around one single mask swapping  protagonist massacring operations run by  the Russian mob  hotline Miami - wrong number darts back  and forth between dozens of characters  and locations this constantly shifting  pace and variety and as hotline Miami -  to be more restrictive in other ways  though you can sometimes choose from a  small selection of weapons or characters  before a level for the most part you're  forced to play the character as the  story sees fit no longer can you choose  the Tony the Tiger mask to silently take  people in every single level instead the  game encourages you to get better at  shooting by forcing you to play as more  run-and-gun characters  [Music]  and what to say about the story well for  one there's a lot more of it the  original game intentionally obfuscated  what was going on behind an unreliable  narrator and secret endings and much of  that continues here callbacks to the  first game ships in perspective along  with furious timeline swapping means  that all of this reads a lot better on a  second playthrough but truly the story  just plays its part in creating a  surreal experience that's best enjoyed  by letting it wash over you hotline  Miami 2 is a challenging often difficult  game but playing through its various  levels is so enjoyable that dying rarely  feels like it's a punishment the game's  grading system gives you an excuse to  return to levels but it's style is an  even more inviting reason to play again  and again the experience is so audio  visually seductive that you'll find  yourself for playing zones just for the  sake of it  the soundtrack sees returning artists  such as perturbator and jasper byrne  supplying a breath of synth and techno  tracks alongside a host of new musicians  and not only is this music as  exceptional as the first game but  there's also a lot more of it in fact  there's a lot more of everything in this  game I completed the original hotline  Miami in about three hours but by the  time the credits had rolled in hot la  Miami too had registered almost 9:00 and  this was before I'd started over with  the unlockable hard mode before I toyed  around at the games level editor which  is currently in the alpha testing stage  in almost every way hotline Miami 2 is a  marked improvement on an already  tremendous formula this is a game that  had me pumping my fists and laughing  with joy throughout my time with it and  I was left despondent by the time it  drew to a close a gutsy refine game that  isn't scared to force you into corners  and watch you battle out of them and an  audio-visual experience that marries  graphics music and designed so well that  even the pause menu is a work of art  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  you

